      THIS PROGRAM IS A LEGACY DATA RECORD SORTING UTILITY
      IMPLEMENTED IN FLOW-MATIC.
      
      INITIATE THE SYSTEM.
      
      OPEN INPUT FILE "DATAFILE.DAT" FOR READING.
      OPEN OUTPUT FILE "SORTED.DAT" FOR WRITING.
      
      MOVE ALL ZEROS TO SORT-FLAG.
      MOVE 0 TO RECORD-COUNT.
      
      BEGIN THE SORT LOOP.
         READ INPUT FILE UNTIL END-OF-FILE.
         IF END-OF-FILE IS EQUAL TO YES,
            EXIT THE LOOP.
         END-IF.
         
         INCREMENT RECORD-COUNT BY 1.
         STORE CURRENT RECORD IN BUFFER.
      END LOOP.
      
      SORT BUFFER BASED ON KEY FIELD.
      
      WRITE EACH RECORD FROM SORTED BUFFER TO OUTPUT FILE.
      
      CLOSE INPUT FILE.
      CLOSE OUTPUT FILE.
      
      TERMINATE THE PROGRAM.
      
      DATA DEFINITIONS.
      
      01 SORT-FLAG.
         05 SORT-FLAG-VALUE PIC 9.
      
      01 RECORD-COUNT.
         05 RECORD-COUNT-VALUE PIC 999.
      
      01 BUFFER.
         05 RECORD-LENGTH PIC 99.
         05 RECORD-DATA PIC X(256).
      
      END PROGRAM.
